    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c36181ce_911f55ab",
        "filename": "service/src/com/android/server/connectivity/PermissionMonitor.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 394,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308473
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-04-07T14:58:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e You add UserHandle.ALL(-1) into mUsersTrafficPermissions when PermissionMonitor starts to monitor. Then add/remove specific user when the user add/remove. I think the UserHandle.ALL will never be removed. Does this mean even all users are removed the permission will still stay since mUsersTrafficPermissions will at least contain UserHandle.ALL and at least one user(UserHandle.ALL) is still available?\n\nYes and no. These syste traffic permission should be always there because it\u0027s native service permission actually.\nDevice will have primary user(UserHandle.SYSTEM) at least. Put these permission to UserHandle.SYSTEM might be a another choice but it will make the design more complicated because we need to consider the permission overwritten problem. So I think put these permission to UserHandle.ALL should be a simple solution. \n\n\u003e If this is true, it seems that add/remove other user is not important at all. The result is sort of decided by the UserHandle.ALL.\nOnly few appIds will apply these permissions. You can refer to frameworks/base/data/etc/platform.xml",
      "parentUuid": "fd02906b_b18d5bfd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 394,
        "startChar": 37,
        "endLine": 394,
        "endChar": 51
